WEBVTT

00:23.090 --> 00:24.470
What's going on?

00:24.470 --> 00:25.960
What is this?

00:25.960 --> 00:28.170
These iceblades are merely emblems;

00:28.170 --> 00:29.450
they are not my true nature.

00:29.450 --> 00:30.500
What?

00:30.500 --> 00:34.380
Give your professor a 
proper answer, Ray White!

00:34.380 --> 00:38.020
These are nothing more than symbols tied 
to the name of the Iceblade Sorcerer.

00:38.020 --> 00:40.930
Make sense, damn it!

00:48.280 --> 00:49.660
Deceleration.

00:50.480 --> 00:53.410
Lock registration!

00:54.900 --> 00:58.040
Why?!

00:58.040 --> 01:00.400
Let's have a lesson, Professor Gray.

01:00.850 --> 01:04.630
What is the biggest difference 
between fire and ice-based sorcery?

01:04.630 --> 01:07.270
What? I'm the professor.

01:07.270 --> 01:08.430
What a foolish query.

01:08.430 --> 01:11.410
The main difference between 
fire and ice sorcery

01:11.410 --> 01:15.220
is whether code is used to accelerate or 
decelerate the particles' vibrations.

01:15.470 --> 01:17.010
That's correct,

01:17.010 --> 01:18.100
I expected nothing less from you.

01:18.650 --> 01:22.130
In other words, ice sorcery 
utilizes deceleration.

01:22.660 --> 01:25.970
Many sorcerers only execute that processing 
on a subconscious level.

01:26.430 --> 01:28.260
But I have created code so intricate

01:28.260 --> 01:30.480
that I am able to control both 
deceleration and anchoring

01:30.480 --> 01:34.070
with such precision that an average 
person could never emulate it.

01:34.350 --> 01:36.940
Then, using antimaterial code,

01:36.940 --> 01:39.270
I am able to reverse the 
code theory itself,

01:39.270 --> 01:41.990
and revert all spells back to prima materia.

01:42.300 --> 01:43.230
What?

01:43.230 --> 01:45.460
Antimaterial code?

01:45.460 --> 01:48.000
But no one's ever done that successfully!

01:48.240 --> 01:50.110
Don't you understand?

01:50.110 --> 01:53.740
Before me, all sorcery returns to the void.

01:54.010 --> 01:57.750
That is the true nature of the 
current Iceblade Sorcerer.

01:57.750 --> 02:00.310
Material shift, ice sword!

02:07.650 --> 02:09.200
Damn it.

02:09.200 --> 02:11.900
I even used the Dark Triad...

02:11.900 --> 02:15.150
This can't be happening!

02:15.380 --> 02:17.100
What kind of sorcery is that?!

02:17.100 --> 02:18.180
I don't know!

02:18.180 --> 02:19.760
Could that be...?!

02:19.760 --> 02:21.780
Mind infiltration sorcery...

02:33.230 --> 02:35.840
Hey, doesn't Ray look odd?

02:36.770 --> 02:38.520
His body...

02:38.520 --> 02:40.340
It's getting covered in ice.

02:50.400 --> 02:54.110
You're not in control 
of your power, are you?

02:58.760 --> 02:59.710
I can do this.

02:59.710 --> 03:00.610
I can do this.

03:00.980 --> 03:03.330
Die, Iceblade!

03:03.330 --> 03:04.150
Ray!

03:09.250 --> 03:11.780
Even if you are the Iceblade...

03:14.130 --> 03:15.710
Ice Bloom Profusion!

03:24.380 --> 03:30.350
No! No!

03:32.810 --> 03:34.040
Wow.

03:40.390 --> 03:43.930
Professor Gray, let's have 
you rest there for now.

03:49.900 --> 03:51.380
Deceleration.

03:53.550 --> 03:56.710
Chronos Lock, activate.

03:57.850 --> 03:58.790
Ray!

03:58.790 --> 04:00.610
Ray!

04:02.670 --> 04:04.330
<i>I protected them.</i>

04:05.040 --> 04:06.590
<i>Nobody was lost.</i>

04:07.410 --> 04:11.840
<i>So it's fine now, right, Master?</i>

04:15.520 --> 04:18.980
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

04:15.520 --> 04:18.980
<b>Episode 5
The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest Sorcerer Has an Unexpected Meeting on the Battlefield</b>

04:20.610 --> 04:22.280
Are you all right?

04:22.760 --> 04:23.990
Hey, hey!

04:26.260 --> 04:28.400
Hang on! I'll save you!

04:34.850 --> 04:37.130
Lydia, who's that kid?

04:37.130 --> 04:39.950
When did you become a mom, Lydia?

04:39.950 --> 04:42.000
Why do you go there, Dumbpink?

04:42.000 --> 04:43.670
I'm still...

04:43.670 --> 04:46.800
Still what, I wonder?

04:49.530 --> 04:51.800
Colonel! Lydia's...

04:54.220 --> 04:57.810
Ainsworth, could you please let 
us know what's going on here?

04:57.810 --> 05:00.760
I heard a voice crying out to me,

05:00.760 --> 05:04.050
so I searched the area and found this child.

05:04.400 --> 05:06.900
It looks like he's the only survivor.

05:07.850 --> 05:10.070
What?! They're refusing to take him in?!

05:10.070 --> 05:12.580
He's a war orphan from this country!

05:12.580 --> 05:16.040
It seems like the village 
he's from is special.

05:16.040 --> 05:17.340
What does that mean?

05:17.340 --> 05:20.460
It's a completely independent 
domain inside the country.

05:20.750 --> 05:23.590
Apparently, the government's stance 
is complete non-intervention.

05:23.590 --> 05:27.000
So they're saying that 
child is not a citizen?

05:27.000 --> 05:28.220
That's ridiculous!

05:30.590 --> 05:32.720
That village is rumored to be cursed.

05:33.330 --> 05:34.470
Cursed?

05:34.760 --> 05:37.570
Something about performing rituals 
to call gods into mediums and such.

05:37.570 --> 05:41.620
Are people really still talking 
about curses and gods?

05:41.930 --> 05:46.900
I mean ceremonies and religion
still exist in the Kingdom, as well.

05:46.900 --> 05:48.790
A dwindling few.

05:49.120 --> 05:51.020
Since the code theory was discovered,

05:51.020 --> 05:55.530
even magic was once considered
supernatural before it became sorcery.

05:55.530 --> 05:57.720
If the research continues at the current rate,

05:57.720 --> 06:00.450
we might even uncover the 
true meaning of the world.

06:00.840 --> 06:05.630
But for people to go on living, 
some things need to be hidden, as well.

06:06.020 --> 06:08.710
I won't deny there are 
psychological benefits.

06:08.710 --> 06:09.700
Oh, right.

06:09.700 --> 06:10.630
What?

06:10.630 --> 06:13.140
I hear he's regained consciousness.

06:13.140 --> 06:15.070
Why didn't you say that first, you idiot?!

06:18.320 --> 06:21.010
And what's your name?

06:23.470 --> 06:24.280
Carol!

06:24.620 --> 06:25.720
Lydia.

06:25.720 --> 06:26.840
What's his status?

06:26.840 --> 06:29.440
He's stable, but...

06:29.840 --> 06:31.390
What's your name?

06:33.430 --> 06:34.850
It's no use.

06:35.860 --> 06:36.760
Ray.

06:37.300 --> 06:38.820
So your name is Ray?!

06:39.360 --> 06:40.260
Yeah.

06:41.370 --> 06:43.030
My name is Lydia.

06:43.030 --> 06:44.790
Lydia Ainsworth.

06:45.670 --> 06:47.040
Lydia...

06:48.090 --> 06:50.350
Let's play ball!

06:50.350 --> 06:51.080
Huh?

06:51.390 --> 06:53.340
Carol, what are you doing?

06:54.390 --> 06:57.340
Becoming great friends 
with Ray, that's what!

06:57.340 --> 06:59.750
Today, I've been reading him picture books.

06:59.750 --> 07:03.260
Ray, can you say my name?

07:03.870 --> 07:04.890
Carol.

07:04.890 --> 07:09.230
But I told you, you can call me Carocaro!

07:09.230 --> 07:11.870
Now, why don't you try saying, 
"I love you, Carocaro"?

07:12.260 --> 07:13.370
Carol.

07:15.390 --> 07:20.120
Ray, it seems you already know how 
this Dumbpink should be treated.

07:21.870 --> 07:25.870
It's not funny, Lydia!

07:25.870 --> 07:26.650
Huh?

07:29.750 --> 07:31.490
He laughed just now.

07:31.490 --> 07:32.650
He laughed, right?

07:32.650 --> 07:35.370
It seemed like that, yeah.

07:36.390 --> 07:40.920
Hey, Ray, I'll tell you about 
my legendary acts of bravery!

07:40.920 --> 07:42.300
Not that again!

07:42.300 --> 07:43.860
Shut up, Dumbpink.

07:43.860 --> 07:45.370
Pffff!

07:48.140 --> 07:51.260
Lydia, about Ray....

07:51.260 --> 07:53.220
Have you found anywhere we could leave him?

07:53.220 --> 07:54.150
No.

07:55.140 --> 07:57.340
What should I do?

07:57.650 --> 08:02.200
You're not thinking of taking him yourself?

08:02.200 --> 08:03.050
Of course not.

08:03.390 --> 08:05.570
We're soldiers.

08:05.570 --> 08:07.700
Of course I wasn't considering that.

08:08.550 --> 08:12.060
But I don't know what that 
Dumbpink will say.

08:12.060 --> 08:13.590
No way!

08:13.590 --> 08:15.550
Ray is staying with me!

08:17.640 --> 08:19.670
Oh, boy.

08:19.670 --> 08:22.610
Caroline, you understand that's
impossible, right?

08:22.610 --> 08:23.910
It is possible!

08:23.910 --> 08:26.720
I have money! I could feed him!

08:26.720 --> 08:28.880
We have a mission.

08:28.880 --> 08:30.970
Then I'll take him to my own house,

08:30.970 --> 08:33.570
but I'm not abandoning him!

08:34.400 --> 08:37.920
I do understand where Carol's coming from,

08:37.920 --> 08:39.070
but there's nothing—

08:39.070 --> 08:40.770
That's not true!

08:40.770 --> 08:42.420
We're sorry.

08:42.420 --> 08:44.100
And what about you two?

08:44.100 --> 08:45.670
As you say, Colonel,

08:45.670 --> 08:48.750
I believe he should be given to an 
orphanage or adopted by someone.

08:49.520 --> 08:51.260
And you, Ainsworth?

08:56.480 --> 08:57.570
I...

08:59.090 --> 08:59.920
Ray.

09:06.770 --> 09:09.130
Ray, what do you want to do?

09:10.700 --> 09:12.970
You heard us talking, right?

09:19.000 --> 09:21.000
I want to stay with you.

09:38.580 --> 09:39.580
Colonel.

09:40.040 --> 09:41.150
What is it?

09:42.460 --> 09:45.670
My family, specifically 
my elder sister's family,

09:45.670 --> 09:48.200
has a daughter close to Ray's age.

09:48.200 --> 09:50.150
Carol and Abbie will help, too.

09:51.170 --> 09:53.140
I will take responsibility for him.

09:53.430 --> 09:57.190
Is there something about Ray that's 
prompted you to go such lengths?

09:57.640 --> 10:02.110
There is, which is exactly why I 
believe he needs proper guidance.

10:03.450 --> 10:04.550
I understand.

10:04.550 --> 10:07.360
So long as this does not affect your 
duties, you have my permission.

10:08.260 --> 10:11.450
Oh, thank goodness!

10:11.450 --> 10:14.600
Ray, you're going to stay with us forever!

10:15.140 --> 10:15.920
Ray,

10:16.840 --> 10:19.210
from now on you'll be staying with me.

10:19.210 --> 10:21.700
No, with us.

10:22.200 --> 10:23.420
Together?

10:23.420 --> 10:24.130
Yeah.

10:25.750 --> 10:26.720
Okay.

10:27.030 --> 10:30.770
Which means that from 
now on, I'm your master.

10:30.770 --> 10:32.120
Master?

10:32.120 --> 10:35.250
That's right! You are my apprentice!

10:35.250 --> 10:38.490
I will be teaching you everything I know.

10:39.010 --> 10:41.950
Okay! Got it, Master!

10:44.120 --> 10:46.200
<b>Six Years Later
 Far East War
 Front Inside the Republic of Merth</b>

10:45.680 --> 10:48.050
Captain, we're done for!

10:48.050 --> 10:50.250
Everyone, retreat!

11:02.290 --> 11:03.900
Icicle Blades!

11:10.160 --> 11:11.720
Complete annihilation confirmed.

11:11.720 --> 11:13.160
Impressive.

11:13.160 --> 11:16.610
All right, then. We'll let the 
soldiers take over after this.

11:16.610 --> 11:19.610
Right, they're waiting for us.

11:21.780 --> 11:24.120
That was a kid, right?

11:24.770 --> 11:29.120
So those are the Arnold Kingdom army's Astrals?

11:29.520 --> 11:30.880
This is Correine.

11:30.880 --> 11:32.260
Subjugation complete.

11:32.260 --> 11:33.250
We're heading back.

11:33.530 --> 11:35.320
Overheating.

11:35.320 --> 11:37.020
What an awful sight.

11:37.020 --> 11:39.110
Excessive use of sorcery,

11:39.110 --> 11:42.180
the stress from being in an environment 
where death is omnipresent...

11:42.640 --> 11:46.870
It's like battlefields were 
designed to cause overheating.

11:47.950 --> 11:51.200
Rampant power that you 
can't control.

11:51.200 --> 11:53.820
The only thing that follows is 
the destruction of your mind.

11:54.210 --> 11:57.110
A disease veritably caused 
by modern sorcery.

11:57.110 --> 11:58.170
Yes.

11:58.170 --> 12:02.700
It can happen to any sorcerer 
on the battlefield.

12:03.100 --> 12:05.410
To anyone.

12:07.600 --> 12:10.500
So, this is the situation at the moment.

12:10.500 --> 12:14.700
The sorcerers Konpeki and Raimei 
have both been confirmed dead.

12:14.700 --> 12:16.240
Of the Seven Grands?!

12:16.240 --> 12:17.960
So there's someone powerful 
enough to do that?!

12:17.960 --> 12:23.470
I suppose that means it's certain that the 
Aywell Empire is intervening in this war.

12:23.470 --> 12:27.540
From here on, the battle lines 
will only get more fierce.

12:27.540 --> 12:31.430
Even us Astrals may not get away unscathed.

12:31.430 --> 12:34.370
I want you all to redouble your focus.

12:34.960 --> 12:37.840
Ray, you are still young.

12:37.840 --> 12:39.780
You could still go back, if you want.

12:40.220 --> 12:41.770
Captain Correine...

12:41.770 --> 12:45.160
That's right. You're the same age as my son.

12:45.160 --> 12:47.820
That's not an age to be on the battlefield.

12:49.620 --> 12:53.780
My master taught me that people 
with talent have a responsibility.

12:53.780 --> 12:56.890
I consider this unit to be like a family...

12:56.890 --> 13:00.070
No, you are my family.

13:00.540 --> 13:03.290
Commander Henrick, Captain Correine.

13:03.290 --> 13:04.880
Colonel Garnet.

13:04.880 --> 13:06.680
Derek, Howard.

13:06.680 --> 13:07.640
Master.

13:07.640 --> 13:09.240
And Carol, I guess.

13:09.240 --> 13:10.320
Ray!

13:10.590 --> 13:12.860
I've prepared for this 
ever since I enlisted.

13:14.660 --> 13:18.280
If anything happens to 
you, I'll come save ya!

13:18.280 --> 13:19.480
Howard...

13:23.390 --> 13:24.740
Howard!

13:28.460 --> 13:29.530
Howard!

13:34.040 --> 13:35.580
Ray, don't!

13:40.840 --> 13:42.080
Howard!

13:43.100 --> 13:45.810
Ray, you go and live.

13:46.310 --> 13:51.400
For now, I'll go up into this 
wide sky and watch you grow.

13:51.400 --> 13:53.460
No, Howard!

13:53.460 --> 13:56.100
Live, Ray.

14:03.180 --> 14:05.060
Ray, are you all right?

14:08.070 --> 14:09.110
Master...

14:11.340 --> 14:12.720
I...

14:12.720 --> 14:14.130
Looks like you used it.

14:14.970 --> 14:16.820
I'm very sorry.

14:16.820 --> 14:18.030
Don't be.

14:18.030 --> 14:20.120
I would have done the same.

14:20.460 --> 14:22.030
Don't worry about it too much.

14:22.030 --> 14:24.720
In the end, it all went well.

14:24.720 --> 14:27.760
At some point, you'll no longer 
need the Chronos Lock.

14:29.130 --> 14:30.730
That reminds me! Everyone...

14:30.730 --> 14:32.220
Is fine.

14:32.220 --> 14:35.030
It seems they only suffered from a 
slight magical energy deficiency.

14:35.030 --> 14:36.990
Everyone's already recovered.

14:37.330 --> 14:39.110
You did well, Ray.

14:50.860 --> 14:53.220
Anyway, I'm glad that you're okay.

14:53.770 --> 14:56.490
Come visit me again when 
you've got some time.

14:56.490 --> 14:58.330
Yes, Master.

14:58.330 --> 14:59.000
Yup.

15:05.240 --> 15:06.270
Miss Carla?

15:07.010 --> 15:08.270
Your ear, please.

15:08.790 --> 15:12.140
Miss Lydia was very worried about you.

15:14.080 --> 15:15.770
Please get some rest.

15:16.170 --> 15:17.300
Good bye.

15:23.500 --> 15:26.580
I was against it, at first.

15:26.580 --> 15:27.150
Huh?

15:27.610 --> 15:29.650
Against you attending the school.

15:30.760 --> 15:34.150
I thought you needed more rest.

15:34.610 --> 15:37.460
Even among the other sorcery 
academies in our country,

15:37.460 --> 15:40.000
ours is especially full of people 
preoccupied with bloodlines.

15:40.410 --> 15:43.170
An ordinary like yourself 
would only be unhappy.

15:43.640 --> 15:46.860
Raised on the battlefield, 
touched by so many deaths.

15:46.860 --> 15:49.680
After all you've been through,

15:50.050 --> 15:54.460
I couldn't stand the thought of 
putting you into an environment

15:54.460 --> 15:56.680
full of the discrimination from the nobles.

15:57.000 --> 15:58.290
Miss Abbie...

15:58.740 --> 16:02.090
But then Lydia came and bowed her head.

16:02.090 --> 16:03.180
My master did?

16:03.550 --> 16:07.930
Her and I go way back, but this was 
the first time she's ever done that.

16:08.630 --> 16:13.200
Ray is even stronger and kinder 
than we ever imagined.

16:13.770 --> 16:17.570
That's why I want him to know 
that there's more to this world.

16:18.480 --> 16:20.780
The good and the bad...

16:20.780 --> 16:25.100
I want him to learn how to feel, 
how to think, and how to live.

16:25.570 --> 16:29.620
What Ray needs now is not us adults,

16:29.620 --> 16:31.540
and especially not the battlefield.

16:32.510 --> 16:36.430
He needs everyday experiences 
appropriate for a boy his age.

16:37.930 --> 16:40.600
Ray doesn't have friends his own age.

16:41.280 --> 16:46.490
I mean, I had you, and I guess Carol.

16:47.580 --> 16:50.250
So that's you want him here?

16:52.710 --> 16:53.850
He...

16:54.820 --> 16:57.330
He deserves to find happiness.

16:58.410 --> 16:59.310
Lydia...

17:00.070 --> 17:02.590
Abbie, please.

17:04.810 --> 17:06.150
Master...

17:15.640 --> 17:20.670
I'm so glad Ray is okay!

17:20.670 --> 17:22.890
I'm glad, too.

17:30.900 --> 17:33.730
Ray, enjoy your life at school.

17:34.270 --> 17:36.500
Find your own happiness.

17:36.500 --> 17:37.900
That is our wish for you.

17:38.680 --> 17:40.370
And Lydia's.

17:43.230 --> 17:44.010
I will.

17:49.210 --> 17:50.350
Go ahead.

17:52.910 --> 17:54.370
You came to visit me.

17:54.660 --> 17:55.430
Sure.

17:55.940 --> 17:58.770
Are you... all right?

17:58.770 --> 17:59.880
Yes.

17:59.880 --> 18:02.370
I see. I'm glad.

18:03.460 --> 18:04.910
Um...

18:04.910 --> 18:05.760
I'm sorry.

18:06.150 --> 18:08.770
I kept my secret from you.

18:09.060 --> 18:12.100
I am one of the seven grand sorcerers,

18:12.100 --> 18:13.940
the Iceblade Sorcerer.

18:15.190 --> 18:17.170
I... see.

18:17.930 --> 18:21.490
Having fought alongside my master 
and the others in the Far East War,

18:22.070 --> 18:25.230
I overheated in the final battle.

18:25.610 --> 18:27.250
Overheated?

18:27.510 --> 18:30.270
It's when you lose control of your engram.

18:30.270 --> 18:33.530
I myself don't entirely understand 
what exactly happened.

18:34.280 --> 18:35.870
But when I regained consciousness,

18:35.870 --> 18:38.050
I saw that everything around 
me had become a wasteland.

18:38.480 --> 18:41.550
My bleeding master had her arms around me.

18:42.460 --> 18:48.160
Even now, I am using a spell called 
Chronos Lock to keep from overheating.

18:48.560 --> 18:51.870
So is this maybe the reason 
you're not so good at sorcery?

18:51.870 --> 18:54.160
That's correct.

18:55.760 --> 18:58.100
I lost many precious friends in battle

18:58.480 --> 19:01.110
and I caused my master grievous injuries.

19:01.380 --> 19:05.370
Of course, even though they were our enemies, 
I took countless numbers of their lives, as well.

19:05.700 --> 19:10.290
I hid my blood-soaked 
past and I deceived you.

19:10.290 --> 19:11.360
I am...

19:12.080 --> 19:14.240
My hands are stained with blood.

19:15.120 --> 19:18.380
Do I have the right to be near you at all?

19:19.650 --> 19:21.430
I've been thinking about it the entire time.

19:22.510 --> 19:23.890
I am truly sorry.

19:32.300 --> 19:35.310
I want you to be here.

19:35.310 --> 19:36.520
Amelia...

19:36.520 --> 19:39.190
No matter what happened in your past,

19:39.190 --> 19:41.630
I believe in the person you are right now.

19:42.020 --> 19:44.710
I know that you are an 
extremely kind person.

19:44.710 --> 19:46.100
That's right!

19:46.100 --> 19:49.350
You're an amazing person and my best bud!

19:49.350 --> 19:52.270
And that's not going to change, 
no matter what happened in your past.

19:52.270 --> 19:55.270
I'll always be with you, too!

19:55.270 --> 19:57.130
I mean, you're my friend!

19:57.130 --> 19:58.070
Jeez.

19:58.070 --> 20:00.940
I can't believe you spent 
time worrying about this.

20:00.940 --> 20:02.700
W-We're friends!

20:02.700 --> 20:03.260
Ray!

20:03.870 --> 20:06.830
We all want to stay with you.

20:06.830 --> 20:09.560
You're not alone.

20:18.450 --> 20:20.780
Thank you, all.

20:33.510 --> 20:34.580
Good evening,

20:35.650 --> 20:37.120
Mr. Alium.

20:37.740 --> 20:39.670
Ray White.

20:40.280 --> 20:42.320
What are you doing here at this hour?

20:44.690 --> 20:46.240
I needed to apologize.

20:47.110 --> 20:50.900
I've done things that can 
never be taken back.

20:51.400 --> 20:53.130
I accept your apology.

20:53.130 --> 20:54.490
It's water under the bridge.

20:54.490 --> 20:56.440
But that's...

20:56.440 --> 21:00.210
You acknowledged your shortcomings 
and delivered an honest apology.

21:00.210 --> 21:02.430
I think that alone is truly amazing.

21:03.110 --> 21:05.440
You really felt that remorse 
deep in your heart.

21:05.750 --> 21:07.870
That's why you're here.

21:08.360 --> 21:10.450
Or am I wrong, Albert?

21:12.320 --> 21:13.370
White...

21:13.810 --> 21:14.820
You can call me Ray.

21:14.820 --> 21:16.240
But...!

21:16.480 --> 21:18.900
That's what I'd like you to call me.

21:20.640 --> 21:23.490
I just can't win.

21:23.490 --> 21:27.060
How can you be so strong and 
never stray from your path?

21:27.330 --> 21:28.310
Ray...

21:28.310 --> 21:34.830
Bloodlines or talent, having those things 
from birth is a wonderful thing.

21:35.270 --> 21:36.590
But that's not everything.

21:37.250 --> 21:40.110
Effort and the right 
environment are necessary, too.

21:40.720 --> 21:43.150
All I did was end up in a good environment,

21:43.150 --> 21:45.840
then simply live day by day.

21:47.270 --> 21:50.540
Shake off your doubts and 
take a new look at yourself.

21:50.870 --> 21:53.420
By now you understand, right?

21:54.030 --> 21:58.220
Once we are aware, 
we can start anything over.

21:58.220 --> 22:02.050
You're the only one who can provide 
yourself with the answer you seek.

22:04.370 --> 22:09.310
What I needed in my life 
wasn't to hate people,

22:09.310 --> 22:10.580
it was to accept people...

22:15.270 --> 22:19.680
You're going to become much 
stronger after this, Albert.

22:20.160 --> 22:22.790
Thank you, Ray.

22:24.710 --> 22:27.510
One of our staff members has 
left us for personal reasons,

22:27.510 --> 22:31.340
so let me introduce you to the new teacher 
who will be replacing Helena Grady.

22:31.340 --> 22:34.240
Why hello there, everyone!

22:34.840 --> 22:38.830
That is right, I will be 
your homeroom teacher!

22:39.300 --> 22:41.770
My name is Carol Caroline!

22:41.770 --> 22:47.980
Feel free to call me Caro, 
or Carocaro, or Miss Carolin.

22:47.980 --> 22:48.960
Teehee!

22:51.460 --> 22:53.960
S-Say what?!

22:53.960 --> 22:58.450
Looking forward to working with you all!

